WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.540
It has risen.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.460
The final Rise of Skywalker trailer is here,
and we've taken a close look at this new footage

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.560
for the Skywalker saga-ending movie.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.920
Here are the small details you may have missed.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.680
In the middle of all of the high-intensity
action, you might have missed the original

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:20.400
Lando Calrissian, played by Billy Dee Williams,
sitting in the center of a massive group of

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.600
Resistance members; a group that also includes
C-3PO, stationed behind Lando, and what looks

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.780
to be Poe Dameron, standing in front of him.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.040
He's sporting a bright yellow shirt similar
to the one a young Lando wore in Solo.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.800
Audiences haven't seen anything of Williams'
version of Lando over the years, but when

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.640
Leia and Larma D'Acy told Poe in The Last
Jedi that there were Resistance allies "scattered"

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.210
in the Outer Rim, many fans took this as a
sign that Lando would make a triumphant return

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.260
before the film series was over, and that
theory has been proven true.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:55.319
We've already seen Lando back in action piloting
the Millennium Falcon in the first Rise of

00:00:55.319 --> 00:00:59.379
Skywalker trailer, but this new footage gives
us a hint at the mission Lando could have

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.519
organized that put him back in the ship he
lost to Han Solo all those years ago.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.460
Could General Lando be taking Leia's place
as the leader of the Resistance following

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.360
her possible death?

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.020
It's something fans have speculated about
since the passing of Leia actress Carrie Fisher.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.600
We can't say for certain, but our interests
are certainly piqued.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.000
If there's one thing the Star Wars franchise
knows, it's how to carry out epic Jedi battles.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.740
From Obi-Wan versus Darth Vader in a fight
to the death, to Luke Skywalker fighting his

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:31.070
own father in a valiant attempt to pull him
away from the dark side of the Force… to

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:31.960
whatever this was.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.720
But in The Rise of Skywalker, there's a fight
that goes down between two complex characters

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:41.030
in a place that's immensely important to the
Star Wars franchise: the ruins of the second

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:46.120
Death Star, the follow-up version of the Empire's
moon-sized weapon ship, which was then destroyed

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.200
in the Battle of Endor.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.960
Why would Rey and Kylo be in the ruins of
the planet-destroying Death Star?

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.740
Well, that's where Emperor Palpatine died,
after being tossed into the Death Star's reactor

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.260
by a repentant Darth Vader.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:01.540
Rey actress Daisy Ridley has promised that
the pale-skinned Sith, otherwise known as

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.620
Darth Sidious, is very instrumental to the
plot of The Rise of Skywalker.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.780
Sounds like the thought-to-be-dead Emperor
might have something that both Rey and Kylo

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.099
are after... which could explain why Rey is
also seen in the final trailer for the film

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.800
confronting Emperor Palpatine.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.299
An epic meeting between Rey and Emperor Palpatine
might be more than just a battle between good

00:02:21.299 --> 00:02:25.870
and evil; many Star Wars fans believe the
Sith Lord could be the rising Jedi's biological

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:26.360
father.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.840
Rey's real parentage has remained a hot topic
of conversation for Star Wars fans - even

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:35.279
after The Last Jedi saw Kylo Ren tell Rey
through clenched teeth that she's the daughter

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.140
of a pair of nobodies who sold her for drinking
money.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.640
From the moment fans heard Emperor Palpatine's
unmistakable cackle in the first Rise of Skywalker

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.500
trailer, speculation that he could be part
of Rey's bloodline took on a life of its own.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.600
Believers of this theory have pointed to the
existence of "dark Rey," seen in the special-look

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.900
footage shown off at D23, as some of the strongest
evidence that Rey has some Sith blood in her.

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.840
Now, even if The Rise of Skywalker doesn't
reveal that Palpatine has any sort of genetic

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.320
connection to Rey, it appears he'll have a
psychological connection with her.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.099
Just as the trailer shows Rey standing opposite
a dark figure that looks like Palpatine, Luke

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:18.919
Skywalker says in voiceover, "Confronting
fear is the destiny of a Jedi." Rey has been

00:03:18.919 --> 00:03:24.249
putting blood, sweat, and tears into becoming
worthy of Jedi status, and by Luke's own word,

00:03:24.249 --> 00:03:27.160
that means her destiny is to look fear directly
in the face.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:31.700
Palpatine could represent Rey's biggest fear:
either learning the truth of her parentage,

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:36.420
or staring down the physical manifestation
of the occasionally-tempting dark side of

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.000
the Force.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.040
At one point, we briefly see Rey and Kylo
Ren both using their lightsabers to take a

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.760
vicious swipe at the statue of Darth Vader's
helmet.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.320
The moment happens quickly, but it still carries
great significance.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:52.760
Not only does this represent the killing of
an era in this galaxy far, far away, but it

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:55.760
also suggests that Kylo may be moving toward
redemption.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:00.360
Though Kylo's donning his own helmet and still
wielding his unique red saber, slicing the

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.459
totem of the person he's spent years trying
to emulate hints at an evolution.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.760
The son of Han Solo and General Leia Organa,
the wayward nephew of revered Jedi Luke Skywalker

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.020
might be the Skywalker who ultimately rises.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:17.140
He has Skywalker blood in him, and he's exhibited
signs of confusion over his alignment within

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:22.070
the Force, so maybe The Rise of Skywalker
will see the Skywalker in Kylo rise above

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:27.280
his dark person, reclaim his birth name of
Ben Solo, and battle against the First Order

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.540
he currently leads.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.000
Even the release date for the final Rise of
Skywalker trailer holds significance.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.980
October 21st is the late Carrie Fisher's birthday.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:41.400
Fisher, who died on December 27th, 2016 after
suffering a heart attack on a flight from

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:46.380
London to Los Angeles four days prior, would
have celebrated her 63rd birthday on the day

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.100
Disney and Lucasfilm unveiled the final trailer.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.780
This holds even more weight when remembering
that The Rise of Skywalker will include footage

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:59.070
of Fisher as General Leia Organa that wasn't
used in 2015's The Force Awakens, in a way

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:03.460
bringing the late actress back to life for
the concluding chapter in the Skywalker saga.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:08.260
Maybe some of the mysteries The Rise of Skywalker
is set to shed light upon will involve exactly

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:12.200
how Leia learned to channel the Force, if
she'll pass the Resistance torch to the next

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:16.240
generation, and whether or not she'll reunite
with her brother Luke on the other side.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:21.280
If director JJ Abrams is to be taken at his
word, The Rise of Skywalker will answer these

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:21.920
questions.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.300
And if the final trailer for the forthcoming
flick is to be taken at face value, fans are

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:31.550
in for something beyond their wildest imagination
when The Rise of Skywalker bows in theaters

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:32.860
on December 20th.

